    "One trail remains, and this profile takes it head on instead of letting it feed confusion. On Deezer, the editorial playlist RAP ANTILLES 2026 files a record by <a href=\"/en/miimii-kds.html\">Miimii KDS</a>, “6 o’clock”, 2 minutes 4, written by Miimii KDS and composed by three names: Joshii, TitoWeGlobal and Jervon Henderson. Joshii, without the Yo. The question writes itself: is that Joshii the same producer as YoJoshii, credited in a short form? No source opened during this research says so. Neither the playlist listing, nor the “SEE U” and “Back Up Your Chat” files, nor any page consulted links the two spellings, and the two names share no documented artist, team or label in common.",
    "The answer of this profile is therefore the only honest one: open trail, separate credit. “6 o’clock” does not enter the list of YoJoshii records carried by this page, nor its story as a fact. It enters as a documented question, because the two names are close, because the two scenes touch, Miimii KDS is a Guadeloupe bouyon artist followed by this site, and because a reader who crosses both credits should know that the link is established by nobody. If a source one day links the two spellings, this page will integrate the record with its date and its full credits, and will say so.",
    "The other neighbouring names settle faster, and they are set aside here so the file stays clean. Yo Joshy is a Martinique shatta artist who sings his own records, among them “Hold Up”: a performer, not the production name of this profile, and no source links him to YoJoshii. Joshii G, for his part, joins this file. On February 15, 2026, the JoshiiMadeIt channel, handle @YoJoshii, posted “What You Up Too Riddim [Bouyon Instrumental 2026]”, credited “prod by Joshii G” and past 320,000 views when read. The same name is executive producer on “Up To”, with <a href=\"/en/gwada-g.html\">Gwada G</a>, <a href=\"/en/nice.html\">Nice</a>, Savage and <a href=\"/en/freddy.html\">Freddy</a>, released on February 21, 2026 on Run Tha Beat Records per the DistroKid listing. He also produces for Vibez King, in a jab and bouyon world. Those set asides are not judgements on those artists: they are acts of credit, of the same kind this site applies to all its producer pages, also to be read on our <a href=\"/en/bouyon-producers.html\">bouyon producers</a> page.",
    "That discipline has a price, and this profile accepts it: the YoJoshii file stays a two credit file. But it also has a benefit, which is the reason this page exists. The day a third credit under the exact name YoJoshii appears, it will be read here with no background noise, no records borrowed from namesakes, and with the same question asked of every line: who opened the source, and what exactly does it say."
